Uncle Bernie's add-ons to DASM:

I've provided the original main.c, global.c, and ops.c as main.org, global.org
and ops.org so you can check if you work with the same version of your source
as I did. The upgraded files are main.c, global.c and ops.c in this tarball.
I've also provided main.ed global.ed and ops.ed which are ed scripts made by
diff.

How to add the features:

in main.c, function parse(), added a code block to reformat the input line into
           something the rest of DASM likes.
           Suggest that this code block should be turned on by a command line
           option, but I had no time to dig any deeper into the code to do this.
           This could prevent misinterpretation of legacy assembly code having
           dubious constructs incompatible with the added features.

in globals.c, MNEMONIC Ops[] = { gets one line more:
    . . . 
    { NULL, v_dc, "dc",  0, 0, {0,} }, <---- copy this line 
    { NULL, v_dc, "dcx", 0, 0, {0,} }, <---- then paste and add 'x' to "dc"
    . . .

in ops.c, function v_dc(), add one line for the 'dcx' directive:

  if(Glen && !strcmp(mne->name, "dcx")) Gen[Glen - 1] ^= 0x80;

This could also be turned off by a command line option but the "dcx" in
global.c must stay, turning it off would be possible but tedious to code.

Test case: run the script 'UBtest' ... no output means all works & matches

(this is the simplest test case ... I actually assemble the whole Microsoft
 6502 BASIC with the upgraded DASM, so I'm confident all my mods do their job)

Permission to use my code snippets from this tgz file in this and future versions of DASM is hereby granted. I regard them as "public domain" stuff and claim
no Copyright on them.

 - Uncle Bernie
